{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011ChK64fPrrxSetQ1qAuQ2e","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Fixed. `slugify('Crème Brûlée')` now returns `creme-brulee`.\n\nThe bug was that the function only lowercased and replaced non-ASCII characters with dashes, so accented letters were split apart. The fix in `slug.js` decomposes accented characters with `normalize('NFKD')`, strips the combining marks, and then applies the existing dash replacement. I also added trimming of leading and trailing dashes. The header comment already promised that behavior, but the code didn't do it; for example `'Hello World!'` previously produced a trailing `-`.\n\nI added two tests to `test/slug.test.js`: one for `Crème Brûlée`, and one for leading, trailing and repeated dashes. `npm test` passes all 3 tests.\n\nLimitation: letters with no decomposition, such as `ß`, `ø` or `æ`, still get dropped. Handling those would need a small transliteration map, which I didn't add since you didn't ask for it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1507,"cache_read_input_tokens":23915,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1507},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2a42ee89-ea4d-4df1-a6c3-ee231cc2e747","uuid":"e21a6fbb-67c2-4b60-9fba-41633dcaa52e","timestamp":"2026-11-23T02:41:27.571Z","request_id":"req_011ChK64fECMGzp6p28XZv6A"}
